※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=64 diag=none

※ A negative exponent written down is refused where it is written.  One the
※ program works out is the same mistake arriving later, so it stops the program
※ the way every other answer that cannot exist does -- and the check is one
※ comparison made once, before the loop rather than in it.
※
※ Only a signed exponent is asked about.  An unsigned one cannot be negative,
※ so asking would be asking a question whose answer is a property of the type.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    raised(2u32, ⁻2i32)

fn raised(x: u32, n: i32) → u8:
    if x ⁿ n ≠ 4u32:
        1u8
    else:
        0u8
